 "input": "Notes from the practice manager on referrals. GP sees the patient and decides they need a specialist. GP writes the referral letter, using the patient record for history and meds. The letter goes through the e-Referral Service, patient gets a booking reference and chooses a hospital and date themselves (or the admin team helps them on the phone). Hospital consultant triages the referral and can bounce it back with advice instead of an appointment. Waiting list is managed by the hospital. After the appointment the consultant sends a clinic letter back, which our admin team codes into the patient record. Practice tracks outstanding referrals on a spreadsheet so nothing falls through the cracks.",
 "expect_status": "ok",
